            "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(\\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i), Y) &\n= & \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(\\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i, v(Y)) \\\\\n& = &\n\\lim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}^{opp}}\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(M_i, v(Y)) \\\\\n& = &\n\\lim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}^{opp}}\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(M_i), Y)\n\\end{matrix}\n$$",
            "MATH_0002": "$u(\\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i)$",
            "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-limit-colim}"
          },
          "render": {
            "prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n",
            "suffix": "\\end{proof}"
          },
          "risk_level": "R3",
          "schema_version": 1,
          "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
          "source_math_hash": "sha256:546a2043499ca7b0b9fbd81c06469cb66f24374356e89cd80fb0fff78028f04c",
          "source_status": "CURRENT",
          "source_structure_hash": "sha256:658f0573c56f7a69f2ed82308b47b0d865e5a621916cc64f10cb68017b932ee4",
          "source_text": "A morphism from a colimit into an object is the same as a compatible\nsystem of morphisms from the constituents of the limit into the\nobject, see Remark <REF_0001>. So\n<MATH_0001>\nproves that <MATH_0002> is\nthe colimit we are looking for.\nA similar argument works for the other statement.\n",
